  "articleBody": "Nobody wants a remodeling project to go sideways, right? So, let's talk about some common pitfalls and how to steer clear of them. A big one is not thoroughly vetting your contractor. Always double-check their licenses, insurance, and ask for references. You want to see similar past work, too, so you know they can deliver on your vision. Another mistake? Not clarifying who's responsible for what. Make sure you know who's supervising the site, managing subcontractors (like plumbers or electricians), and handling all the paperwork. At HH Remodeling, Abraham is often the principal contact and on-site lead, so you always know who's in charge. It's also super important to get a clear picture of the projected timeline and how changes will be handled. Projects can evolve, and a good contractor will have a clear process for change orders. By avoiding these missteps, you set yourself up for a much smoother and more satisfying remodeling experience. If you’re in Denver or the surrounding areas like Centennial or Parker, give us a ring at 303-505-0866; we're happy to walk you through our process!",
  "datePublished": "2026-08-09"
